title: mf repo root
tags: [[CLI command]] Daemon
kind: reference
summary: Print the selected repository's root (an absolute path)

Prints the root of the repository `-n`/`-u` names, as the daemon reports it
(`GET /repos/:repo`, [[Repository endpoints]]), without a trailing `/`.

It is for scripts that act on many records: read the root once, read every
record's relative path in one call (`mf metarecord -q … get --resolve-tree
mfr_path --tsv`), and join them. `mf path` gives the same absolute path
for one record, but at one daemon call per record. The tagging scripts do this
through `mf_gui_read_root` and `mf_gui_abs_path` ([[lib/mf-gui.sh]]).
